# flow-update
flow update adt $DIR/adt.json
flow update-all $DIR/all.json
flow update adt
--- stdout
{"id":"adt","name":"ADT Inbound","sourceType":"","status":"undeployed","enabled":true,"destinations":[{"name":"out","type":"file","dir":"$DIR/out"}]}
{"updated":["adt"]}
--- stderr
Error: usage:
flow subcommands:
  flow list
  flow get <id>
  flow create <file>
  flow update <id> <file>
  flow update-all <file>
  flow rename <id> <name>
  flow enable|disable <id>
  flow remove <id>
  flow export <file> [<id>...]
  flow import <file> [--overwrite]
  flow deploy|undeploy|start|stop|pause|halt|resume <id>
  flow redeploy-all
  flow deploy-all|undeploy-all|start-all|stop-all|pause-all|halt-all|resume-all
  flow start-destination|stop-destination <id> <destination>
  flow connectors
  flow ports
  flow stats [<id>]
  flow reset-stats <id> [lifetime]

<id> is a flow id or name; quote arguments with spaces: "ADT Inbound".
--- exit 2
